Fibonacci Numbers with Caramel Sauce.
This recipe prints the first N Fibonacci numbers, where N is the initial
amount of flour. It uses an auxiliary recipe for caramel sauce to define
Fibonacci numbers recursively. This is a corrected version of the classic
recipe from the Chef specification, which returns 1 for every call and
never actually recurses as published.

Ingredients.
5 g flour
250 g butter

Method.
Sift the flour. Put flour into mixing bowl. Serve with caramel sauce. Stir the
mixing bowl for 1 minute. Fold butter into the mixing bowl. Rub the flour until
sifted. Pour contents of the mixing bowl into the baking dish.

Serves 1.

Caramel Sauce.

Ingredients.
0 g count
0 g result
0 g temp
1 g one

Method.
Fold count into mixing bowl. Clean mixing bowl. Put count into mixing bowl.
Remove one from mixing bowl. Fold temp into mixing bowl. Simmer the temp. Put
count into mixing bowl. Remove one from mixing bowl. Remove one from mixing
bowl. Fold temp into mixing bowl. Heat the temp. Put count into mixing bowl.
Remove one from mixing bowl. Serve with caramel sauce. Fold result into mixing
bowl. Clean mixing bowl. Put count into mixing bowl. Remove one from mixing
bowl. Remove one from mixing bowl. Serve with caramel sauce. Fold count into
mixing bowl. Clean mixing bowl. Put count into mixing bowl. Add result.
Refrigerate. Toast until heated. Clean mixing bowl. Put one into mixing bowl.
Refrigerate. Bake until simmered. Clean mixing bowl. Put one into mixing bowl.
